-- title:
--   Orbit parametrization undoes the full-shell inverse on the norm shell
-- statement:
--   For $N\in\mathbb{N}$ and a Gaussian integer $z$ in the full norm shell (norm $a^2+b^2=4N+1$, entries in $[-(2N+1),2N+1]$), applying the Jacobi orbit parametrization to the data $(i,(r,s))$ extracted by the full-shell inverse returns $z$: $\mathrm{orb}(\mathrm{inv}(z))=z$. Together with the previous statement this gives a bijection used in Chapter 15.
-- source:
